{number: 109}
{title: Face to Face with Christ}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Face to face with Christ, my Savior,
Face to face—what will it [F7] be,
When with [Bb] rapture I be-[Eb] hold Him,
Jesus [Bb] Christ Who [F7] died for [Bb] me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bb] Face to face I [F7] shall behold Him,
Far beyond the starry [Bb] sky;
Face to face in all His [Eb] glory,
I shall [Bb] see Him [F7] by and [Bb] by!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Only faintly now I see Him,
With the darkling veil be-[F7] tween,
But a [Bb] blessed day is [Eb] coming,
When His [Bb] glory [F7] shall be [Bb] seen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
What [Bb] rejoicing in His presence,
When are banished grief and [F7] pain;
When the [Bb] crooked ways are [Eb] straightened,
And the [Bb] dark things [F7] shall be [Bb] plain.
{end_of_verse}
